WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:00.943
- I'm just thinking about,

00:00:00.943 --> 00:00:02.920
well I'm thinking about a lot
of stories and things that

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:03.753
happened you know.

00:00:03.753 --> 00:00:05.480
I remember when we were together,

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:07.960
you had your amazing dogs,

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:10.740
Flossy and Templeton,

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:11.950
and Vivian.
- Yeah.

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:14.610
- I remember one time it was Christmas,

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:18.190
and you came up to Canada to my parents'

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:21.030
house for Christmas, and,

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:25.160
I flew Flossy up to Canada for Christmas

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:26.520
and didn't tell you,

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:29.580
you were sitting on the floor
of the house that I grew up in

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:33.620
as a kid, and I opened the
door and Flossy walked out,

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:36.890
and I remember you looking at Flossy,

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:37.723
and you thought,

00:00:37.723 --> 00:00:39.231
"Oh, there's a dog that
looks like Flossy."

00:00:39.231 --> 00:00:41.120
And then you realized it was Flossy,

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:42.840
and it was very cute.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.876
And so, I sort of had this
lifelong love of dogs now,

00:00:45.876 --> 00:00:49.710
because of Flossy and
Templeton and Vivian, yeah.

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:52.500
- Well, we had that house fire,

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:57.400
and Flossy saved us and
got us out of the house,

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:00.000
and we're standing up
on the top of the hill.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.640
The house was in the canyons.

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:03.491
And when I'm watching the,

00:01:03.491 --> 00:01:08.491
telephone poles explode,
and the house was a barn,

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:10.960
it was built out of wood, wood,
floors, walls, and ceiling.

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:12.800
So it went like an Acme cartoon.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:13.633
It just sort of like,

00:01:13.633 --> 00:01:15.710
the fire went through the
house and then it crumbled.

00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:17.770
And I was just standing
there in such shock,

00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:20.097
and I was looking down and just going,

00:01:20.097 --> 00:01:22.720
"Okay I just hope this doesn't
ravage anybody else's homes.

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:25.480
Like this one's gone and that's that."

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:28.998
And you leaned into my ear
and you started singing,

00:01:28.998 --> 00:01:32.100
♪ Da na na na na na na na na na ♪

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:34.130
The Entertainment Tonight theme.

00:01:34.130 --> 00:01:36.969
And it's like when your whole life--

00:01:36.969 --> 00:01:39.220
- Well I think the media
had assembled outside

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:40.053
in front of the house.

00:01:40.053 --> 00:01:42.437
It was obviously a horrible situation.

00:01:42.437 --> 00:01:44.196
- But it made me laugh--
- I felt so bad.

00:01:44.196 --> 00:01:47.090
- In that moment that
everything was so dark,

00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:48.370
and scary and confusing,

00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:49.630
and you lightened it up for me.

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:51.330
You made me laugh.

00:01:51.330 --> 00:01:53.044
And I will never forget that.

00:01:53.044 --> 00:01:57.450
In the middle of what was
such a terrifying moment,

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:00.370
there's this one little light in it.

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:03.808
And it's you making me giggle so hard,

00:02:03.808 --> 00:02:07.430
in the middle of this
darkness came this light,

00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:08.672
and it was you.

00:02:08.672 --> 00:02:12.990
We just had so many crazy adventures and,

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:17.130
in some ways having lived such
a public life, my whole life,

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:21.380
I still was in new territory
with what you were doing with

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:22.334
yours.

00:02:22.334 --> 00:02:24.930
You were bringing cameras into everywhere.

00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:26.850
Nobody was doing this.

00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:28.170
This was not...

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:30.730
Not only, not normal in the funnest way,

00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:32.920
but it was unprecedented.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:35.390
I mean, you've been
doing podcasts for years,

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:37.210
before podcasts were a thing.

00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:40.060
And now you're taking
a podcast, on the road.

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:41.059
- Right now I've just...

00:02:41.059 --> 00:02:44.450
Charlie and I we're about to
go take off on an adventure,

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:45.283
crew.

00:02:45.283 --> 00:02:48.370
We're going across the country in a van.

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:50.930
Charlie and I are moving
into a van next week.

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:53.609
And we're gonna go out into the beautiful,

00:02:53.609 --> 00:02:55.640
emptiness of America,

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:57.180
lots of places that people haven't been,

00:02:57.180 --> 00:03:00.150
some of the beautiful places
that people don't get to see,

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:02.653
and I'm gonna be doing my
podcast out of this van.

00:03:02.653 --> 00:03:06.110
And, kind of much like
what you're doing here,

00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:09.670
this burst of optimism and
positivity that you bring to TV

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:10.503
every day.

00:03:10.503 --> 00:03:13.100
I kinda wanted to do something
where we went out and

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:17.740
celebrated, the great things
about America, right now,

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:20.370
'cause there's a lot of
negativity in the world and,

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:22.100
I became an American citizen last year.

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:22.933
I don't know if I told you that.

00:03:22.933 --> 00:03:23.835
- Congratulation.

00:03:23.835 --> 00:03:24.680
(audience cheers and claps)

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:26.080
- So,

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:26.913
yeah.

00:03:26.913 --> 00:03:27.746
So--

00:03:27.746 --> 00:03:28.579
- And it's a better country for it.

00:03:28.579 --> 00:03:29.412
- I made it.

00:03:29.412 --> 00:03:31.030
- Thank you Tom.

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:32.320
- Do you like my mug?

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:34.170
- I do. Oh my God.

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:36.239
Is that me with a neck brace on?

00:03:36.239 --> 00:03:37.683
- Oh,

00:03:37.683 --> 00:03:38.680
(Drew laughs)

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:39.513
Oh,

00:03:41.210 --> 00:03:42.043
Oh yeah.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:45.120
- Oh my God.
- Oh yeah.

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:46.500
That's you with a neck brace on.

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:47.899
I found this...

00:03:47.899 --> 00:03:49.270
(Tom giggles)

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:52.690
I found this mug in my
garage, a couple years ago

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:53.740
and I just kinda kept it,

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:55.970
'cause I figured someday
I might be on your TV show

00:03:55.970 --> 00:03:58.800
and it'd be fun to have
a sip out of the mug.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:00.220
- Well, the tables have turned,

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:02.375
now I have the cameras on you Tom.

00:04:02.375 --> 00:04:03.320
- Yup. Yup.

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:06.710
Remember the day in New
York, you were doing yoga,

00:04:06.710 --> 00:04:07.766
you sprained your neck.

00:04:07.766 --> 00:04:08.599
- Yeah.

00:04:08.599 --> 00:04:10.130
- And then Chris went and made...

00:04:10.130 --> 00:04:13.780
Chris made these mugs, and somehow,

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:14.861
I kept the mug.

00:04:14.861 --> 00:04:18.049
all these years, I've kept the mug, so.

00:04:18.049 --> 00:04:20.010
- I'm so happy to see you.

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:23.650
And in the words of Patty
Smith, we were just kids.

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:24.500
- Yes. Yes.

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:25.620
We were.

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:29.120
We were in our twenties, and,

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:33.550
now I'm not in my twenties anymore, but--

00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:35.176
- Where does the time go?

00:04:35.176 --> 00:04:38.370
- Yeah, we had a lot of
amazing, amazing experiences,

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:42.570
and I'm grateful for that
and I cherish them and,

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:44.088
thanks Drew, I appreciate it.

00:04:44.088 --> 00:04:46.090
- I cherish you right back.

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:46.930
- Thanks drew.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:48.405
- Thank you Tom.

00:04:48.405 --> 00:04:53.150
I wanna mention that the Tom
Green interview on Apple,

00:04:53.150 --> 00:04:57.670
Spotify, or wherever you
listen to podcasts is out.

00:04:57.670 --> 00:04:59.390
It will be available.

00:04:59.390 --> 00:05:04.390
I suggest you go through a
library of Tom Green when,

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:08.930
you need it most or you
just wanna feel good.

00:05:08.930 --> 00:05:10.064
All right?

00:05:10.064 --> 00:05:12.647
(upbeat music)

